  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "The graph of $y=x^2$ is transformed to $y=9x^2$. Bob says that it was vertically dilated, whereas Mary says that it was horizontally dilated. Who is correct, and why?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p24-q11-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Both are correct: vertical factor ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "9",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " or horizontal factor ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac13",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q11-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "9x^2=(3x)^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", so multiplying the output by 9 or replacing x by 3x gives the same rule.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Both are correct.\n\nFor a vertical dilation by factor $9$, replace $y$ by $\\frac{y}{9}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{9}&=x^2\\\\y&=9x^2.\\end{align*}$$\nFor a horizontal dilation by factor $\\frac{1}{3}$, replace $x$ by $\\frac{x}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=3x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(3x)^2\\\\y&=9x^2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth transformations produce the given graph.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
